The fix involves checking the short GI support based on the current bandwidth being used (80MHz, 40MHz, or 20MHz) and the corresponding capability information elements. This ensures that the driver only sets the short GI capability if it is supported for the actual bandwidth in use, thus preventing incorrect transmission settings.

